/-- This theorem states that for any type α and any two functions f and g mapping from α to the complex numbers, the sum of the functions (fun x ↦ f x) and (fun x ↦ g x) is equal to the function which maps each x to the sum f x + g x.-/
private lemma fun_add {α : Type*} (f g : α → ℂ) :
  (fun x ↦ f x) + (fun x ↦ g x) = fun x ↦ f x + g x := by sorry

/-- This lemma claims that for any real number x and functions f and g mapping real numbers to complex numbers, the value of their sum at x is equal to the sum of their individual values at x.-/
private lemma eval_add (f g : ℝ → ℂ) :
    (f + g) x = f x + g x := by sorry

